note:
Customs of a Serbian wedding:
• guests are invited with a small bottle of ра̏кија;
• the сва̑тови go to the bride's house for her, and the column is led by a барја̀кта̄р with a flag;
• the bride wears a венчаница and a veil;
• the groom must shoot an apple down;
• the bride throws a glass: whether it breaks or not predicts the sex of the child;
• after the civil ceremony the newlyweds step on each other's foot - whoever is first will be the boss;
• the bride is carried over the threshold, she throws a sieve onto the roof and knocks over a vessel of water.
